{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll 3 tests pass. Here's a summary of what was changed:\n\n**`app/repository.py`** — Migrated all queries from `session.query()` to SQLAlchemy 2.x `select()` constructs. Removed `session.commit()` from `create_entry()` so the caller manages the transaction boundary.\n\n**`app/api.py`** — `create_ledger_entry()` now calls `session.flush()` instead of relying on a repository-level commit, keeping the transaction open for the caller's `begin()` context.\n\n**`app/worker.py`** — `settle_entry()` wraps the full mark-and-settle sequence in a try/except with `session.rollback()` on failure, so a failed settle never leaves stale `\"processing\"` state. `settle_batch()` uses per-entry transactions.\n\n**`app/admin_cli.py`** — `plan_batch()` now calls `session.rollback()` on `dry_run=True` instead of committing. `reconcile_batch()` uses per-entry transactions with the same dry-run rollback semantics.\n\n**`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`** — Updated to document the actual migration instead of the old \"keep the shim\" guidance."}}
